 "lang": "en",
 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "Three American aircraft carriers now sit off Iran. And Tehran says it won't wait."
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "The newest is the USS Theodore Roosevelt. Axios, citing a U.S. official, reports it has arrived. It joins the George H. W. Bush and the George Washington, mostly in the Arabian Sea. Gulf News calls it the biggest U.S. naval presence there since April."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Iran answered through deputy foreign minister Kazem Gharibabadi. He told the state news agency IRNA that Tehran will not wait for America to attack first. He accused Washington of using talks to buy time for a new military operation."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Iran International, citing the New York Times, reports that U.S. and Israeli planners are weighing strikes on Iran's economy. President Trump has called the war militarily over. But the U.S. blockade of Iranian ports goes on."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will America and Iran trade new strikes before December? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
