 "upload": {
  "title": "3 US Carriers Near Iran. Is a New Strike Coming? #shorts",
  "description": "A third U.S. aircraft carrier strike group has reached the Middle East. The USS Theodore Roosevelt has arrived in the region, Axios reported citing a U.S. official; Gulf News said it entered U.S. Central Command's area of operations on Sunday, November 15, 2026. It joins the carrier strike groups of the USS George H.W. Bush and the USS George Washington, which have been operating mainly in the Arabian Sea. According to Gulf News, three carriers is the largest U.S. naval presence in the region since April. Iran's deputy foreign minister Kazem Gharibabadi told the state news agency IRNA that Tehran \"will not wait for the US to attack first\" and accused Washington of possibly using diplomatic talks to buy time for a new military operation. Iran International, citing the New York Times, reported that U.S. and Israeli planners are weighing possible strikes on Iran's economic infrastructure; it remains unclear whether any decision has been taken. U.S. President Donald Trump said on November 9 that the war was \"militarily effectively over\"; the U.S. naval blockade of Iranian ports remains in place. No official U.S. response to Gharibabadi's remarks had been reported at the time of production. Carrier positions in the video are approximate.\n\nSources:\nAl Jazeera live, Nov 16, 2026: Third US carrier arrives, Iran warns it could strike first\nGulf News, Nov 16, 2026: US-Iran tensions surge as third aircraft carrier enters Middle East\nHaaretz (citing the New York Times), Nov 16, 2026: Reports: Third U.S. aircraft carrier deployed to Middle East\nTimes of Israel liveblog (citing Axios), Nov 16, 2026: Third US aircraft carrier said to arrive in Mideast\nIran International liveblog, Nov 14–16, 2026\nCBS News, Nov 9–10, 2026: Trump says Iran war \"militarily effectively over\"\n\n#geopolitics #Iran #USNavy #Hormuz #MiddleEast",
